{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:ce2e6ec7024a6f33","name":"ET-74 Communications Droid","source":{"id":"source:reference-ce2e6ec7024a6f33","title":"ET-74 Communications Droid","revision":19126,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:22:04Z","sha256":"192ebcafc33abbd53e0c2a5c78f5543f676756cd70b928f6751f3556ec108e16","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=19126","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=ET-74%20Communications%20Droid&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-ce2e6ec7024a6f33","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Developed by Automata Galactica to handle communications in automated facilities and coordinate the efforts of Labor Droids, the ET-74 Communications Droid is a multipurpose Droid that handles electronic communication and logistics for several different industries. The ET-74 Communications Droid is programmed with an excellent mastery of computer systems and networks, as well as a variety of data transmission and receiving systems. Additionally, this Droid has several routines that enable it to communicate effectively with its biological masters, making it an excellent liaison between a large Droid worker force and their living owners.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["ET-74 Communications Droids are small and often found on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Stations"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Stations","referenceId":"reference:65763f09c9074f45"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["Capital Ships"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Capital_Ships","referenceId":"reference:a08d2e2cd508d403"},". Though they are no match for a living communications officer, these Droids can temporarily replace crew members by manning the communications and sensor stations for a short while. ET-74 Communications Droids put in charge of mining, construction, and excavation Droids whose tasks are menial (requiring ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droids"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droids","referenceId":"reference:6e72e583603b9ea8"}," with only a marginal intelligence) but which require coordination to ensure that a task is completed. As a result, some beings confuse ET-74 Communications Droids for Worker Droids of various types, though in truth they are merely directing those Droids under their charge.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["ET-74 Communications Droids can be played as ",{"tag":"a","children":["Droid Heroes"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Droid_Heroes"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["ET-74 Communications Droid Statistics (CL 0)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Small ",{"tag":"a","children":["1st-Degree Droid"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/1st-Degree_Droid"}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 1\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +1; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +0\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Binary"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Binary","referenceId":"reference:ee1c8277caf5fb9b"},", 5 Unassigned; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Translator Unit"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Translator_Unit","referenceId":"reference:0bcd4b383b11cac0"}," (DC 10)\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},